{"name":"Parrot Feather","hex":"#a9a237","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parrot feather","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of parrotfeather."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parrot_feather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Myriophyllum aquaticum","blocks":[{"text":"Myriophyllum aquaticum is a flowering plant, a vascular dicot, commonly called parrot's-feather and parrot feather watermilfoil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Myriophyllum_aquaticum_-_side_%28aka%29.jpg/330px-Myriophyllum_aquaticum_-_side_%28aka%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myriophyllum_aquaticum","wikidata":"Q899338"},{"title":"Parrot","blocks":[{"text":"Parrots, also known as psittacines from the name of the type genus Psittacus, are birds with a strong curved beak, upright stance, and clawed feet. They are classified in four families that contain roughly 410 species in 101 genera, found mostly in tropical and subtropical regions. The four families are the Psittaculidae, Psittacidae, Cacatuidae (cockatoos), and Strigopidae. One-third of all parrot species are threatened by extinction, with a higher aggregate extinction risk than any other comparable bird group. Parrots have a generally pantropical distribution with several species inhabiting temperate regions as well. The greatest diversity of parrots is in South America and Australasia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Rainbow_lorikeet_%28Trichoglossus_moluccanus_moluccanus%29_Sydney.jpg/330px-Rainbow_lorikeet_%28Trichoglossus_moluccanus_moluccanus%29_Sydney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parrot","wikidata":"Q31431"},{"title":"Feather","blocks":[{"text":"Feathers are epidermal growths that form a distinctive outer covering, or plumage, on both avian (bird) and some non-avian dinosaurs and other archosaurs. They are the most complex integumentary structures found in vertebrates and an example of a complex evolutionary novelty. They are among the characteristics that distinguish the extant birds from other living groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg/330px-Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather","wikidata":"Q81025"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Starr_070515-7059_Myriophyllum_aquaticum.jpg/500px-Starr_070515-7059_Myriophyllum_aquaticum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Starr_070515-7059_Myriophyllum_aquaticum.jpg/1280px-Starr_070515-7059_Myriophyllum_aquaticum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Starr_070515-7059_Myriophyllum_aquaticum.jpg/500px-Starr_070515-7059_Myriophyllum_aquaticum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStarr_070515-7059_Myriophyllum_aquaticum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parrot_range_2026.png/500px-Parrot_range_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parrot_range_2026.png/1280px-Parrot_range_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parrot_range_2026.png/500px-Parrot_range_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org